# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and blocked by the
# pre-commit hook in `.githooks/` — enable it with:
#
#   git config core.hooksPath .githooks

# The only secret this project has. Used exclusively by the local pipeline.
#
# It must never reach the frontend. Phase 0 of this project was removing a
# `define` block in vite.config.ts that injected this key into the browser
# bundle, where anyone loading the page could read it. CI now greps the built
# output for it on every push.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# There is deliberately no model setting here.
#
# This file used to offer GEMINI_PRIMARY_MODEL and GEMINI_SECONDARY_MODEL.
# Nothing read either of them. Models are chosen by `QuotaLedger.choose_model`
# from the `MODELS` tuple in ai/quota.py, which pairs each id with its
# published RPD and RPM — and that pairing is the point: a model pinned by
# environment variable would have no quota row, so the limiter would not know
# what it was allowed to spend. Change the ids in ai/quota.py instead.

# Optional. Local SQLite storage. Both are gitignored; neither should ever be
# committed, as the first holds unredacted listing data.
#
# DB_PATH is a full SQLAlchemy URL rather than a filesystem path, despite the
# name — it goes straight to `create_async_engine`. Left unset it resolves
# against the project root, so it does not depend on the working directory.
#
# This file previously documented it as DATABASE_URL, which nothing reads:
# setting the documented name did precisely nothing while the default quietly
# kept working. That is the kind of wrong that survives for a long time.
# DB_PATH=sqlite+aiosqlite:///sentinel_blocket.db
#
# QUOTA_LEDGER_PATH *is* a path, and a relative one, so it does depend on the
# working directory. launchd starts jobs in `/`, which is why
# scripts/nightly.sh sets it absolutely.
# QUOTA_LEDGER_PATH=quota_ledger.db
